  "content": {
    "id": "v2-11f0f-p40-practice-slot-2-lower-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A water jet in a fountain at a Brisbane park follows the path $y=-0.5x^2+4x+1$, where $y$ is the height above the water, in metres, and $x$ is the horizontal distance from the nozzle, in metres. A footbridge is 10 metres above the water.\nDetermine whether the jet will hit the footbridge.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. Setting $10=-0.5x^2+4x+1$ gives $\\Delta=-2<0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10&=-0.5x^2+4x+1\\\\0.5x^2-4x+9&=0\\\\\\Delta&=(-4)^2-4(0.5)(9)\\\\\\Delta&=-2<0\\end{align*}$$\nThere are no real solutions, so the jet never reaches a height of 10 metres and does not hit the footbridge.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
